#X text 18 103 Click in the box to the left in the object to turn on/off the DSP:;
#X text 23 279 Notice that if you use the the above message \, [pddp/dsp] still responds to the change in DSP status. [pddp/dsp] also responds to the keyboard shortcuts.;
#X text 138 343 On Mac OS X: Cmd-. and Cmd-/;
#X text 47 329 On Windows and GNU/Linux: Ctrl-. and Ctrl-/;
#X obj 34 142 pddp/dsp;
#X text 16 182 [pddp/dsp] is basically a fancy version of this:;
#X text 16 39 [pddp/dsp] is a GUI object to turn on and off the audio processing \, aka "DSP". It also shows the status of the DSP \, green means DSP is on \, grey means DSP is off.;
